ROI categories live in `roi.categories` (`RoiCategory`, `roi.categories.CategoryRepository`).
The database owns labels, ordering, default lag/ranking and `allows_time`; the survey
catalog filters on that flag. New categories require data, not a Python enum.
- Lead timezone (2026-11-10): `simpl_core.utils.lead_timezone.resolve_lead_timezone(lead_location=, company_location=, company_city=, company_country=)` -> `LeadTimezone(timezone, source)` | None reads where a lead is from LinkedIn-style text and company codes (US states/postal codes, Canadian and Australian regions, metro names; the last country named wins; a bare postal code counts only when the company is not outside the US); `country_code(text)` turns a country name or ISO2/ISO3 code into ISO2. `services.lead_timezone.refresh_lead_timezone(session, lead_id)` stores it on `sales.lead.timezone` / `timezone_source` (writes only on a change, never commits); simpl-outreach calls it before every walk. The email claim and the light-move claim gate on `sales.ulc_send_window` (the ICP's sending hours in the lead's zone, simpl_api migration 20261110150000), not on the seller's active hours; tests open a lead's window with `tests.active_hours_windows.open_lead_window(session, ulc_id)`.
